An additional bounded diagnostic builds each unchanged source with GCC14 and
Clang19 at -O0 -g -static -no-pie, launches an owned child, then three times
stops it after 150 ms, reads selected globals via /proc/<pid>/mem, and resumes.
Each child is killed and reaped after diagnosis (termination -9, NOT PASS).
The binary symbols/addresses and hashes are recorded separately for each build.
No source instrumentation, g_5 write, changed seed or raised benchmark budget.

base/239: both compilers observe g_5=0x6544d187 and g_7=-10 in all three samples.
Earlier PC samples reach func_73 lines 709–717. The loop initializes g_7=-10,
tests g_7<17, updates only a local XOR accumulator, then takes goto lbl_445 on
the unchanged nonzero g_5 before g_7's update. There is no call or pointer store
in this body. Its safe shift helper returns its left operand for this excessive
count; the subsequent 8-bit divide by 0x51 gives zero, leaving the accumulator
unchanged too. Sampling establishes the reaching state; the source transition
shows why it repeats. The finite control also checks the terminating g_5=0 case.

Both /466: prior samples reach func_2's finite body (lines 203–271). New samples
show table g_130[3][4]=1, g_130[0][3]=1, g_130[0][2]=-10, g_468=1 and
g_375=&g_130[0][3] for both compilers. g_668 ranges through its reset/increment
cycle while g_534/g_477 remain zero. This is NOT an infinite inner for loop:
func_2 returns during those outer loops' first iteration. Caller func_1's
constant-safe-shift condition is nonzero (lines 89–95), copies *g_375 to g_468,
calls func_2 with &g_130[3][4], then restarts if g_668 is nonzero.

At that observed state, func_2 resets g_668 to zero and initially breaks on the
nonzero table element. (*p_3)^20 is true. Its bounded eight-iteration body
increments g_668 eight times, sets *g_375=1, and ORs zero into g_468 (the
constant 0xc6de9556 has low bit zero). Therefore the true branch executes the
finite 28,25,...,4 loop and stores the comparison result 1 back to *p_3;
the huge uint64 constant exceeds g_668. The function returns, its caller sees
g_668=8 and restarts in the same controlling state. No alternate func_4 call is
reached on this path. The finite reduction covers zero/nonzero initial table
states (g_668=16/8), preserves the separated pointee/guard addresses, and adds
fuel only to the reduction. It does not modify any original benchmark loop.

Both C-HIR and EvoIR return zero; GCC14/Clang19 O0/O2 and EvoCC O2 assembly all
exit zero. Clang's tautological-large-constant warning is retained. The first
local invocation omitted the sysroot and got E0105; using the same existing
ARM64 sysroot as the lane resolves that setup error, not a compiler fix.
The only new C file is the finite regression; no production code changes.
The original denominator remains 1,000, with 932 agreeing, zero mismatch and
68 oracle-unusable. These three diagnostic terminations add no checksum PASS.

